Boudewijn mentioned playing polypileless.  The table above
gives the odds from death-drop, found-on-floor, in-shop
and from polypile.  Since elves and hobbits both have
chances of being created with elven daggers and assorted
soldier types have chances of being created with regular
daggers, the number of silver daggers found in the
dungeon is *much* smaller.

If you don't genocide the types of monsters that come
with initial items, you can end up with vast numbers of
those items.  Ludios alone can give you 10+ regular
daggers.  So can the Castle.  The mines can give you
20+ elven daggers.  Early on there are so many orcs that
orcish daggers can be treated as expendable items.  But
no type of monster comes with a chance of a silver
dagger.  They only appear as random items in initial
inventories, on the floor, etc.  A zrufy is as likely to
give you a silver dagger as a hobbit is, strangely enough.
(If I read the spoilers and sources correctly).



